  "rationale": "The device failed to correctly identify a clinically significant ventricular tachycardia episode in real time, resulting in a missed detection. While the event self-resolved and no adverse outcome was recorded, this represents a serious potential patient safety risk as sustained ventricular tachycardia can be life-threatening if not promptly addressed. The consistency of the confidence score log, clinician read, and waveform export suggests a systemic issue rather than an isolated anomaly. This necessitates investigation to determine the root cause and prevent recurrence.  The device incorporates software, triggering obligations under EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.2 regarding software development lifecycle and cybersecurity, as well as 21 CFR §820.10(c) concerning design controls for devices automated with computer software. Furthermore, MDR Annex I, Section 17.1 requires that electronic programmable systems ensure repeatability, reliability, and performance in line with their intended use, and that appropriate means are adopted to mitigate risks in the event of a single fault condition.",
